# Tools that are run manually for developmer tasks or run by Bazel
# but not used by tests or at runtime.
#
# tools.txt has NO pip_compile Bazel target (see ../requirements/BUILD, which
# only defines runtime.txt and all.txt), so nothing regenerates it for you and
# it silently drifts. Regenerate it with the command recorded in its own
# header, which is:
#
#   uv pip compile bazel/requirements/tools.in \
#     -c bazel/requirements/runtime.txt \
#     --overrides=bazel/requirements/overrides.txt \
#     -o bazel/requirements/tools.txt
#
# Both flags matter. Without `-c runtime.txt` these tools resolve standalone,
# which is a resolution no build ever performs: all.in pulls `-r tools.in` into
# all.txt, where runtime.txt's pins constrain them. Without `--overrides` the
# security floors do not apply here at all. Dropping `-c` in particular lets the
# unbounded `mcp>=1.28.1` override float to a new major, because tools.in has no
# fastmcp to cap it the way all.txt does.
# Floor raised to 9.14.1 for CVE-2026-34726 / CVE-2026-34730 (template root
# escape and _external_data path traversal).
copier>=9.14.1
# Pinned EXACTLY: the monolith imports pysemgrep's INTERNAL ScanHandler /
# core_output / rule_match APIs (projects/monolith/semgrep_scan/report.py) to relay
# fc-invoke findings to the Semgrep AppSec Platform, and this pin must match the
# fc-invoke Pro engine version so fingerprints line up. Bumping this version
# REQUIRES re-verifying the pysemgrep import surface in report.py (see the
# version-coupling comment there) before merging.
semgrep==1.168.0
